## Content System Checklist

When working with content systems:
- [ ] All required fields have safe defaults
- [ ] All numeric values are clamped to safe ranges
- [ ] All string fields are checked for empty/null
- [ ] All arrays are type-checked before iteration
- [ ] Missing templates fall back to default template
- [ ] Validation errors are logged with context
- [ ] Invalid data never crashes the game
- [ ] Config files are valid JSON/CFG format
- [ ] Changes are tested in-game before committing

---

## Summary

Data-driven content allows rapid iteration without code changes. Always validate input data, provide safe defaults, and never crash on malformed data. The game should gracefully degrade and log warnings when content is missing or invalid.
